    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for openssh",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for openssh fixes the following issues\n\nSecurity fixes:\n\n- CVE-2026-3497: information disclosure or denial of service due to uninitialized variables (bsc#1259642).\n- CVE-2026-35388: omitted connection multiplexing confirmation for proxy-mode multiplexing sessions (bsc#1261441).\n- openssh potential security issue when validating mac or ciphers (bsc#1264568).\n\nOther fixes:\n\n- Improve %prep LDAP regex to preserve subdirectories (e.g., openbsd-compat/) and handle optional [ab]/ prefixes.\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SL-Micro-6.2-1057",
        "title": "Patchnames"
